msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:6
msgid "minios-image-builder - customize MiniOS as a verified image"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "USAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:8
msgid "\\f[B]minios-image-builder\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:8 en/minios-image-compose.1:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:15
msgid ""
"\\f[B]minios-image-builder\\f[R] launches MiniOS Image Builder, a GTK "
"project workspace for remastering MiniOS through \\f[B]minios-image-"
"compose\\f[R](1).  It selects and fingerprints a MiniOS source, lets the "
"user select source and additional \\f[B].sb\\f[R] modules, creates a secure "
"build plan, and structurally verifies the private ISO before publishing it."
"\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:26
msgid ""
"The application runs inside MiniOS and never source-builds MiniOS or "
"modifies source media.  The source can be the current session, a MiniOS ISO "
"file, or an optical disc.  ISO and optical-disc sources are mounted read-"
"only through \\f[B]udisksctl\\f[R].  The application and composition remain "
"unprivileged.  A fixed path-bound helper reads \\f[B]/etc/live/"
"config.conf\\f[R] only when it is root-only; optional writable-session "
"capture authorizes only trusted \\f[B]savechanges\\f[R](1).\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "WORKFLOW"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]Source\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:33
msgid ""
"Select the current livekit or dracut session, a MiniOS ISO file, or an "
"optical disc asynchronously.  The page shows backend, media category, source "
"path, release, version, architecture, bootloader, size, module counts, and "
"diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]Content\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:40
msgid ""
"Select source modules and add external \\f[B].sb\\f[R] files.  Required core "
"and kernel modules remain selected and locked.  Active modules outside the "
"source media are shown separately and are not included automatically.  "
"Basename and target collisions block continuation.\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]Settings\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:54
msgid ""
"Select output identity, allowlisted system defaults, boot behavior and PNG "
"appearance, an optional root-relative project filesystem layer, and optional "
"session capture.  Security, user-data, and expert kernel controls remain in "
"compact expanders.  Empty or Keep current values preserve source behavior.  "
"Inclusion of \\f[B]/etc/live/config.conf\\f[R] is currently required.  Its "
"bytes are read and copied verbatim, frozen during planning, and staged mode "
"0600 in the private build job.  Its values are not interpreted, displayed, "
"or logged.  A loaded \\f[CR]include_current_config=false\\f[R] value is "
"preserved but blocks Review.\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]Review\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:66
msgid ""
"Create a fresh build plan and show selected, deselected, and additional "
"modules, output defaults, path-free customization intent, capture mode and "
"privilege boundary, size estimates, warnings, and stable diagnostic codes.  "
"Configuration values, raw kernel arguments, private customization paths, and "
"selected capture paths are never shown.  An existing output is replaced only "
"after confirmation and a new backend plan bound to the same observed file "
"identity.  Cancellation, failure, or an identity mismatch clears approval, "
"so every retry asks again."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]Build\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:73
msgid ""
"Revalidate every effective input, execute \\f[B]minios-image-compose\\f[R] "
"with list-based argv in the backend\\[cq]s descriptor-bound working "
"directory, capture writable changes when requested, structurally verify "
"customization and capture attestations, and publish atomically only after "
"verification succeeds.\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "IMAGE CUSTOMIZATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:80
msgid ""
"System controls cover hostname, timezone, default target, and enabled or "
"disabled services.  Security and access controls expose only backend-"
"allowlisted sudo, polkit, SSH, XRDP, X11, lock-screen, and issue-hint "
"modes.  User data can link or bind user directories, but not both, and "
"accepts a validated root-relative user-directory path."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:85
msgid ""
"Boot controls preserve or set a 0-300 second timeout and default resume/new/"
"choose/fresh/toram session.  Expert kernel arguments are validated for "
"bootloader-safe syntax.  Boot backgrounds must be valid PNG files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:93
msgid ""
"The project filesystem layer is an existing canonical real directory, or a "
"mode-0700 directory created by the backend beneath the project directory.  "
"The tree is copied relative to image root.  No scripts, raw shell, chroot, "
"or package commands are exposed, and the source directory is never deleted.  "
"Reusable modules belong in Module Manager."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:101
msgid ""
"Review presents only override key names, boot settings, kernel byte count "
"and SHA-256, background basename/digest, and overlay basename/fingerprint/"
"counts.  Successful verification presents the corresponding attested summary "
"and overlay module size/hash.  Composition is unprivileged; authorization is "
"limited to the fixed config reader and optional session capture."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "CANCELLATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:114
msgid ""
"Inventory, build, and verification subprocesses run in dedicated process "
"groups.  Inventory cancellation requests an identity-bound private backend "
"marker before sending \\f[B]SIGTERM\\f[R], then escalates to "
"\\f[B]SIGKILL\\f[R] after a short grace period.  Build cancellation signals "
"\\f[B]minios-image-compose\\f[R], whose trap owns its internal capture "
"marker.  Pure Python hashing may finish its current pass before cancellation "
"reaches a safe checkpoint; stale results are discarded and close waits for "
"tracked work.  Atomic publication is not cancelled after it starts, so the "
"destination is never intentionally left half-written.\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "REQUIREMENTS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:127
msgid ""
"The composition backend is provided by the matching \\f[B]minios-image-"
"compose\\f[R] package, guaranteed by an exact package dependency.  Session "
"capture additionally uses \\f[B]savechanges\\f[R] from \\f[B]minios-"
"tools\\f[R] 1.5.0 or newer.  \\f[B]pkexec\\f[R] is required; a desktop "
"polkit agent is recommended for root-only current configurations and non-"
"root session capture.  \\f[B]udisksctl\\f[R] from \\f[B]udisks2\\f[R] is "
"required for ISO-file and optical-disc sources.  Capture is enabled only "
"after a successful savechanges version probe.  The launcher prefers "
"distribution-owned \\f[B]/usr/bin\\f[R] tools over local shadows.\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "PROJECTS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:134
msgid ""
"Projects are JSON documents written through the ImageProject backend.  Use "
"the header actions or \\f[B]Ctrl+N\\f[R], \\f[B]Ctrl+O\\f[R], "
"\\f[B]Ctrl+S\\f[R], and \\f[B]Ctrl+Shift+S\\f[R] to create, open, save, or "
"save as.  Unsaved changes require confirmation before closing or replacing "
"the current project.\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:141
msgid ""
"Capture mode, normalized selected paths, compression, and sensitive-capture "
"acknowledgement are project intent.  Session inventories are runtime-only "
"and are never written to project files.  Exact acknowledgement is stored in "
"the project and remains in effect until revoked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:146
msgid ""
"Customization fields are also project intent.  Older projects without them "
"load Preserve source defaults.  Save As preserves absolute output, "
"background, overlay, and module targets while invalidating plans when "
"project base changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:146
#, no-wrap
msgid "CAPTURE MODES"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]Current composition\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:153
msgid ""
"Use selected source modules and current configuration without writable-"
"session capture.  Composition is unprivileged; a root-only current "
"configuration may require authorization for the fixed packaged reader."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:153
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]Exact session\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:159
msgid ""
"Preserve writable changes supported by the detected OverlayFS or AUFS "
"provider.  This union-specific mode may preserve secrets, identities, "
"personal files, and logs, and requires explicit acknowledgement."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:159
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]Privacy-cleaned\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:165
msgid ""
"Use the strict software and safe-default allowlist.  Broad system, identity, "
"cache, log, and user state is intentionally omitted.  This is not a "
"guarantee that the result is shareable."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:165
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]Selected changes\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:173
msgid ""
"Capture at least one normalized path selected from an analyzed inventory.  "
"Selecting a directory represents descendants; \\f[B]savechanges\\f[R] "
"enforces actual matching.  Advanced include/exclude editors expose all "
"loaded rules.  Exact and ancestor exclusions override matching row selection."
"\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:173
#, no-wrap
msgid "SESSION INVENTORY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:180
msgid ""
"Analyze session changes is an explicit action.  It creates a private "
"mode-0700 workspace, obtains narrow savechanges \\[en]inventory-json argv "
"from the backend, uses pkexec only when authorization is needed, validates "
"the mode-0600 result, and removes the workspace by device and inode "
"identity.  Command output and private paths are not logged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:196
msgid ""
"The inventory contains metadata, not file content, but filenames are "
"sensitive.  It remains in memory only.  The interface shows aggregate union, "
"entry, byte, category, sensitive, exact-default, and privacy-cleaned-default "
"counts.  Selected paths appear only in the in-memory selector; Review shows "
"count and digest.  The selector materializes 500 rows at a time with a 2,000-"
"row hard display cap and reports displayed, matching, and total counts.  "
"Search is debounced and filters the complete inventory.  Reanalysis, Source "
"refresh, cancellation/failure, and new/open project transitions clear "
"inventory, search, filters, and displayed rows while preserving loaded "
"selection rules.  Successful Selected-changes attestation repeats the Review "
"selection count and verified digest."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:196
#, no-wrap
msgid "BOOT TESTING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:201
msgid ""
"After a successful build, the application can report that external boot "
"testing is available when an installed VirtualBox or QEMU executable is "
"detected.  It does not install, recommend, configure, or invoke a hypervisor."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-image-builder.1:201
#, no-wrap
msgid "RELATED COMMANDS"
msgstr ""

